solutions.latex:
The box-plot indicates a symmetrical distribution. The cumulative frequency diagram increases at a decreasing rate up to the inflection point, and after this increases at an increasing rate. Histogram C has frequencies that decrease towards the centre at a decreasing rate and then increase at an increasing rate, so C is correct.

A is incorrect. The same frequency is added throughout, so the cumulative frequency diagram would be a diagonal line.

\exfigure{277_q9_s1}

B is incorrect. Its cumulative frequency diagram would increase at an increasing rate then at a decreasing rate.

\exfigure{277_q9_s2}

